:02:05","deltaSeconds":422}}},"historicalRank":{"fieldSizeRank":37,"finishersRank":37,"finishRateRank":83,"winningTimeRank":6,"winningTimeRankDir":1,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"menRecords":["up"],"menPreviousRecord":{"time":"05:25:33","holder":"Vladimir KOTOV","year":2000,"type":"up"},"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1959,"mensWinner":"Trevor ALLEN","mensTime":"06:28:11"}},"narrative":"The 2008 Comrades Marathon was the 83rd running of the race, run in the 'up' direction from Durban to Pietermaritzburg over 86.940 km. The race was held on Sunday, 13 June. Conditions: Cool and mild at start. Mild sunshine with localised cloud cover in parts. Runners had 12 hours to complete the course.\n\nLeonid SHVETSOV claimed the men's title in 05:24:49, ahead of Jaroslaw JANICKI (05:38:29) and Stephen MUZHINGI (05:39:40). Elena NURGALIEVA won the women's race in 06:14:37, followed by Olesya NURGALIEVA (06:15:52).\n\nLeonid SHVETSOV's 05:24:49 set a new up record, beating Vladimir KOTOV's 05:25:33 from 2000. Elena NURGALIEVA's 06:14:37 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1959 (Trevor ALLEN, 06:28:11).\n\nFrom a field of 11,185 entries, 8,634 runners crossed the finish line (77.2% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 7,221 men and 1,413 women (16.4% female). The average finish time was 10:09:07.\n\nMedals awarded: 20 Gold, 420 Silver, 1,552 Bill Rowan, 3,960 Bronze, 2,682 Vic Clapham. 1,648 runners (19.1%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Herman VERHAGE in 11:59:59.\n\nCompared to the previous up run in 2006, the field was 7.2% smaller.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 51% of the finishers, with 4,219 seniors (avg 09:50:17) and 4,415 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}